Enable env-backed u-boot bootcount on BPI-R4 (A/B rollback foundation).

With CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT + _ENV + _ALTBOOTCMD, autoboot increments a
boot counter stored in the u-boot env (gated by the `upgrade_available`
env var, so normal boots neither count nor write flash) and runs
`altbootcmd` instead of `bootcmd` once the counter exceeds the env
`bootlimit`. This is the mechanism the A/B slot-switch logic builds on.

Enabled on all three R4 media defconfigs so the mechanism can be
validated quickly on the SD u-boot (fast reflash) before being wired
into the eMMC product env.

--- a/configs/mt7988a_bananapi_bpi-r4-pro-4e-emmc_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7988a_bananapi_bpi-r4-pro-4e-emmc_defconfig
@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@
 CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=1
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_KEYED=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR=" "
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD=y
 CONFIG_OF_SYSTEM_SETUP=y
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE="mediatek/mt7988a-bpi-r4-pro-4e-emmc.dtb"
 CONFIG_SYS_CBSIZE=512
--- a/configs/mt7988a_bananapi_bpi-r4-pro-4e-sdmmc_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7988a_bananapi_bpi-r4-pro-4e-sdmmc_defconfig
@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@
